# rfc9774-as-set-api-not-advertised -- RFC 9774 Section 3 send, on the API
# announce rail.
#
# RFC 9774 Section 3: "BGP speakers: MUST NOT advertise BGP UPDATE messages
# containing AS_SETs or AS_CONFED_SETs".
#
# VALIDATES: the fixture plugin below issues, over ze's own command dispatcher,
#   send bgp * update hex attr set 4001010040020A01020000FDF20000FDF3
#           nhop set 0A000001 nlri ipv4/unicast add 18C00002
# (ORIGIN IGP, AS_PATH holding one AS_SET {65010 65011}, 192.0.2.0/24), then a
# clean fence announce of 198.51.100.0/24. The eBGP receiver gets a withdrawal of
# 192.0.2.0/24 in place of the set route, then the fence: no frame carries the set
# segment, and the warning names the RFC section and the fix. The producer is
# internal/test/fixture/register_rfc9774_api_announce.go.
# PREVENTS: an API-supplied attribute block putting an AS_SET on the wire.

stdin=peer:terminator=EOF_PEER
option=timeout:value=20s
option=bind:value=0.0.0.0

# Receiver (AS 65002). First the withdrawal the guard writes in place of the set
# route. This rail does not track what the peer holds, so the withdrawal of a
# never-held prefix is not suppressed; it announces nothing.
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF001B02000418C000020000
# Then the fence: ORIGIN, AS_SEQUENCE [65000] ze prepended, NEXT_HOP 10.0.0.1,
# 198.51.100.0/24. An UPDATE announcing 192.0.2.0/24 fails the sequence at seq=1.
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=2:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF002F02000000144001010040020602010000FDE84003040A00000118C63364

# No frame carries the set segment, prepended or not.
reject=bgp:conn=1:pattern=01020000FDF20000FDF3
EOF_PEER

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external rfc9774-api-announce {
		run "le test fixture plugin/rfc9774-as-set-api-not-advertised"
		encoder json
	}
}
bgp {
	peer receiver {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 65000
				remote 65002
			}
			router-id 1.2.3.4
			family {
				ipv4/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
			}
			capability {
				graceful-restart disable
			}
		}
		attach process rfc9774-api-announce {
			send [ update ]
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=le test peer --port $PORT:stdin=peer
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=20s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=RFC 9774 Section 3 forbids advertising an AS_SET or AS_CONFED_SET
reject=stderr:pattern=panic
reject=stderr:pattern=fatal error
